885:  * fgets(stdin) cannot be used here: NSH leaves the console in raw mode, so
886:  * Enter arrives as '\r' and never as '\n' — fgets() would block forever even
887:  * though bytes are being delivered.  Reading the raw fd and accepting both
888:  * '\r' and '\n' as the line terminator works regardless of the termios state.
889:  *
890:  * Returns the line length (may be 0 for an empty line) or -1 on a fatal error.
891:  */
